# Implementation Plan - Phase 3: SmartCart Optimization

# Goal Description
Implement the core "SmartCart" optimization engine. This deterministic algorithm takes a consumer's shopping list and location, then outputs the optimal combination of stores to minimize cost (including delivery fees and distance), while strictly avoiding "Dynamic Pricing" or "Surge Pricing" as per regulations.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Algorithm Privacy**:
> The algorithm requires user location. We must explicitly request consent *before* calculating distance-based optimization.
> - **Input**: `UserLat`, `UserLng`, `CartItems[]`.
> - **Constraints**: Max 3 stores per order (to prevent logistical nightmares).

> [!WARNING]
> **Distance API Costs**:
> Google Distance Matrix API is expensive ($10/1k).
> - **Strategy**: Use **Haversine Formula** (straight line) for initial filtering, then only call Distance Matrix for the final 3 candidate stores. This keeps us in the free tier.

